// Signing for `make ios-install-device`, which installs a build on your own iPhone with a free
// Apple ID (Xcode's "Personal Team"). Copy to Device.xcconfig (gitignored) and fill in both
// values; see "Installing on your iPhone" in apps/ios/README.md.
//
// Only that command reads this file, and it applies these values over the configuration it
// builds (Prod-Release by default), so the committed Dev, Staging, and Prod settings stay as
// they are for the paid Apple Developer account.

// Your Personal Team id: 10 characters, shown in Xcode > Settings > Accounts > your Apple ID
// (the team "Your Name (Personal Team)"), or printed by `make ios-install-device` when unset.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// A bundle id prefix only your Apple ID uses. A free team cannot register an id another team
// owns, such as com.listora.app. The app is this id, the Share Extension this id plus ".share",
// and the App Group "group." plus this id, all derived from it.
// For example: com.yourname.listora
BASE_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER =
